{"text": "\u201cPCD,\nVOLE LLL a\n\u2018Tobacco Company\n\n910-741-5000\nWinston-Salem, N.C. 27102\n\nSeptember 20, 1995\n\nDear Fellow Employees:\n\nIn my August letter to you concerning President Clinton\u2019s proposal to give the\nFood and Drug \u2018Administration broad authority over cigarettes, I promised to\nprovide you with a summary of the proposed regulations and information on how\nto voice your opinions to the FDA.\n\nEnclosed is a brochure with highlights of the FDA proposal and the impact it\nwould have on smokers and on the tobacco industry. Please review the\ninformation and use it when talking with friends and relatives about the issue.\nThis brochure will also be sent to RJR retirees and to thousands of friends of\ntobacco across the country asking them to voice their opinions to the FDA and to\nCongress.\n\nThe FDA\u2019s 90-day comment period ends Nov. 9. I urge you to write the FDA as\nsoon as possible and voice your opinion. Also, it is important to send a copy of\nyour letters to your congressmen in Washington.\n\nThe brochure also includes addresses and procedures for writing to the FDA. You\ncan also find this information in the September issue of Caravan and on\nTargetVision.\n\nDuring the week of Oct. 2, the Tobacco Action Coalition plans to organize a\nletter-writing campaign to make it easier for every employee who wants to write\nthe FDA and Congress to do so. TAC will also have petitions available for you to\nsign.\n\nI don\u2019t have to tell you again the drastic effects the president's proposal would\nhave on our ability to sell cigarettes to adult smokers. Yet, the president and the\nFDA have worked very effectively with the media to position their goal as that of\n\u201cprotecting the young people of the United States from the awful dangers of\ntobacco.\u201d While we agree that children should not smoke, the government's\nproposal goes far beyond the issue of youth smoking. The real goal of this\nproposal is to further regulate the tobacco industry and severely limit the choices\nof 45 million American adults who choose to smoke.\n\n- over -\n\n\u201cWe work for smokers.\u201d\n\n\u20acLSS 6oLts",
